nning."]}, "overview": "First-term Republican Monica De La Cruz faces a serious challenge from Tejano music star Bobby Pulido in a South Texas district redrawn to be more Republican. Most race raters call it a tossup, though several recent ratings have moved toward Democrats, and prediction markets give Pulido roughly an 85% chance. Polls since the summer consistently show Pulido ahead, with the most recent independent survey putting him up seven.\nPulido has outraised the incumbent and benefits from a favorable national environment and signs of Latino voter movement away from Trump-era Republicans. De La Cruz retains the structural advantage of an R+7 district and has drawn heavy outside Republican spending against her opponent. The race remains genuinely competitive, but the weight of recent evidence points to a narrow Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4454, "margin": -0.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6234, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6548, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6308, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6942, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6077, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6479, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7065, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6601, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6541, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6766, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6611, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6572, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6619, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6805, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6513, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6318, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6525, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026